'''Politics of Balboa''' takes place within the framework of a {{w|unitary state|unitary}} {{w|presidential republic}}, established by the [[Constitution of Balboa|1974 constitution]] following the country's [[Reunification of Balboa|reunification]]. The constitution provides for a directly elected [[President of Balboa|president]] as {{w|head of state}} and {{w|head of government}}, a vice president elected on the same ticket, and a unicameral [[National Assembly of Balboa|National Assembly]]. The constitution incorporates the [[Twelve Guarantees]] as entrenched provisions that cannot be amended or repealed without the consent of the [[Adonian Community]].

Balboa's political system has historically been a {{w|dominant-party system}} under the [[Balboan People's Party]] (BPP), which has held the presidency and a legislative majority for most of the period since reunification. However, the BPP's dominance has declined significantly in the 2020s, with the party losing its Assembly majority for the first time in 2024 amid competition from socialist, populist, and regional parties.

== Government structure ==

=== Executive ===

{{main|President of Balboa}}

The president is the {{w|head of state}} and {{w|head of government}} of the Republic of Balboa. The president is elected by {{w|two-round system|direct popular vote}} for a five-year term and may serve a maximum of two consecutive terms. If no candidate receives an absolute majority (50%+1) in the first round, a {{w|runoff election|runoff}} is held between the top two candidates within 21 days.

The vice president is elected on the same ticket as the president and assumes the presidency in the event of vacancy. The vice president has no independent constitutional role beyond succession and such duties as the president may assign.

The president appoints the [[Cabinet of Balboa|cabinet]], subject to confirmation by the National Assembly. The president may {{w|veto}} legislation, but the Assembly may override a veto by a three-fifths majority. The president is the {{w|commander-in-chief}} of the [[Balboan Defence Forces]] but may not deploy the armed forces domestically without Assembly authorisation, except in cases of direct invasion or insurrection. The president may not rule by decree; all executive actions must have a basis in statute or the constitution.

The current president is [[Lim Hui-jin]], a Fosian-descended Balboan elected in the [[2025 Balboan presidential election|2025 election]].

=== Legislature ===

{{main|National Assembly of Balboa}}

The National Assembly ({{lang|ca|Assemblea Nacional}}) is the unicameral {{w|legislature}} of the Republic of Balboa. It consists of 120 members, elected by {{w|single transferable vote}} (STV) from multi-member constituencies corresponding to the five provinces. There is no electoral threshold, allowing small parties and regional movements to win representation.

The Assembly operates on a system of {{w|staggered elections}}: half of the seats (60) are contested every two years, with each member serving a four-year term. This means the entire Assembly is never replaced at once, providing continuity while ensuring regular electoral accountability. The staggered system also means that the president's political mandate and the Assembly's composition may diverge, as presidential elections (every five years) and Assembly elections (every two years) operate on different cycles.

The [[Third Guarantee]] of the [[Twelve Guarantees]] requires that a minimum number of seats in the Assembly be allocated to representatives of the former mandate territory, ensuring that the Black and mixed populations of the Sant Cristòfor region have guaranteed representation regardless of provincial electoral outcomes. The minimum seat allocation is set within the overall 120-seat total.

The Assembly's powers include:
* Enacting legislation
* Approving the national budget
* Confirming presidential cabinet appointments
* Overriding presidential vetoes (three-fifths majority)
* Authorising the domestic deployment of the armed forces
* Impeaching the president (two-thirds majority)
* Calling [[snap elections]] with a three-fifths vote of no confidence

=== Judiciary ===

{{main|Judiciary of Balboa}}

The Balboan judiciary is a three-tier system consisting of:

* '''Courts of first instance''' — trial courts with general jurisdiction over civil, criminal, and administrative matters, organised by province
* '''Supreme Court of Balboa''' ({{lang|ca|Tribunal Suprem}}) — the court of final appeal for all non-constitutional matters, including civil, criminal, and commercial cases
* '''Constitutional Court of Balboa''' ({{lang|ca|Tribunal Constitucional}}) — the court with exclusive jurisdiction over constitutional questions, including the interpretation and enforcement of the [[Twelve Guarantees]]

The Constitutional Court consists of nine justices appointed for non-renewable twelve-year terms. Three justices are appointed by the president, three by the National Assembly, and three by the Supreme Court from among its own members. The Constitutional Court has the power of {{w|judicial review}} and may strike down legislation or executive actions that violate the constitution, including the Guarantees.

Under the [[Twelfth Guarantee]], the [[AC Tribunal]] in the [[International City of Areza]] has jurisdiction over disputes concerning the interpretation and enforcement of the Twelve Guarantees. The Balboan Constitutional Court hears Guarantees cases at first instance, but its rulings may be appealed to the AC Tribunal, which has the final authority on Guarantees matters. The AC Tribunal may also take direct jurisdiction in cases involving serious or systematic violations of the Guarantees, bypassing the domestic courts.

=== Local government ===

{{main|Administrative divisions of Balboa}}

Balboa's administrative structure comprises four levels of government. Every citizen resides within a province, a comarca, and a municipalitat; the ciutat and districte levels exist only in certain urban areas.

==== Provinces ====

Balboa is divided into five provinces — [[Tramuntana Province|Tramuntana]], [[Nurra Province|Nurra]], [[Jala Province|Jala]], [[Estret Province|Estret]], and [[Migjorn Province|Migjorn]] — each with an elected provincial assembly and a directly elected governor. The governor serves as the chief executive of the province and is responsible for provincial administration, infrastructure, and the coordination of comarca-level services. Provincial assemblies are elected by STV every four years and have legislative authority over matters devolved to the provinces by the national constitution, including education, health, and provincial transport.

